WEBVTT

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:10.100
Good morning, church. Good morning. It's great to see all of you here. If we haven't met yet,

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.400
my name is Pete. I'm one of the pastors here at HMCC, and I'm excited to share God's Word

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.740
with you this morning. If you want to open to Ephesians chapter 1, that's where we're

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:23.160
going to be looking today. And also just especially welcome those of you who are new today to

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.640
our church community. Really glad that you are here, just getting connected, checking

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.140
out what God is doing here, hopefully getting connected to our community, and hopefully

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:35.240
it'll be a good day for that. As Solomon mentioned, it is fall break. A lot of our college students

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.720
who are a big part of our church life are away at our undergrad retreat, and so let's continue

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.800
to pray for them as they finish up and get back here. But this morning, you know, I kind of look

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:49.060
forward to these opportunities when, you know, people are away, and really I get to speak to

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.720
some of you in our church community that aren't part of our college ministry. I look forward to

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.400
these times, and so we're going to get into that here this morning. Before we get started with

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:02.980
today's message, I do just want to take a moment to acknowledge that what we talked about last week

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:08.700
was kind of a lot. It's pretty heavy. And if you weren't here, if you're new to our church,

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.980
you're not sure what we're talking about, go to our church website, hmcc.net. You'll see a link

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:17.700
there. You'll see what we're talking about. But we had to talk about our former pastor's misconduct,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:23.640
and that's a lot to deal with, a lot for us as a church together, a lot for many of us personally

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:29.220
to go through. Some of you feel more directly impacted by that, just because of close relationships

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.380
or history. Some of you, maybe on your own experiences, feel impacted by that. Some of you

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:38.360
are like, man, that's sad, but, you know, kind of happens, and let's go on with life. There are a lot

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:43.140
of different responses to that. I want to take a moment here just to kind of share a couple

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:47.400
comments about that before we get into today's message, because I realize it is going to take

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:53.440
some continual walking through things. I specifically want to mention that, well, first of all, today

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.540
is not part two of what we talked about yesterday. So if that's kind of what you're thinking

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:02.880
it will be, today's not that. But I do want to share some thoughts. First thing is I just

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.680
want to acknowledge, some people shared after last week that bringing up our former pastor's

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:12.820
misconduct brought up some personal experiences for you. Maybe at a different time or place

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:17.400
in life, maybe in a different church, maybe even in childhood. And I just want to share

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.880
that if you're going through something, that's what the church is for. And please feel free

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:26.240
to talk to one of our prayer ministers, talk to myself. We would love to pray with you and support

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.660
you at the very least as you go through that, and you don't have to go through that alone.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.060
This is what the community of the church is for. Also, we do have Christian counselors in our area

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:39.260
who we partner with and we refer people to, and if that's something that would be helpful to you,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.180
we would love to make those connections and even support you in the process. So I just want to

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.580
mention those things up front, because I know that that is what some of us are going through.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.920
But also, I just want to mention that, you know, over the past week, I've gotten so many emails,

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:58.300
texts, different kinds of messages from people. And I'm thankful for all of that. There's been a

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:03.020
broad range of things people have shared, but I'm thankful for all of it. I heard from a lot of

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:10.360
people that I haven't talked to or heard from in like 10, 20, 25 years who reached out. And for

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:16.740
many of them, they were sharing just supportive and encouraging messages. Also sorrow, of course,

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.280
because it's a tragic situation. But many people also just express thankfulness that we're trying

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:27.520
to deal directly with these things. And I'm very thankful for those messages of encouragement.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:33.340
I also want to just share, even for our encouragement here, many people pointed out to me that most

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:39.100
churches wouldn't do and don't do the things like we did. Just trying to directly and clearly apply

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:44.860
the scriptures to an uncomfortable and sad and tragic situation. And I think many people appreciated

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:49.500
that and affirmed our church with that. And I think that's something that we can feel good about for

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:54.740
our church community in the midst of a really hard situation that we're going through. And so I'm

00:03:54.740 --> 00:04:00.700
thankful for all those messages of support, but also many people have reached out and shared messages

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:10.400
of grief, of anger, of just hurt, of suspicion toward our church. And I just want to acknowledge

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.980
that as well. I've received probably 10 times as many messages of support, but you know, I also

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:21.420
realize for those people who do come forward and share their hurt, their anger, their suspicion,

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.680
their things like that, there are probably many more who feel those things and haven't said

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:31.420
anything to us. And I just want to acknowledge, as I said last week, there are so many reactions

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:36.420
and so many different responses to these kinds of things that we're going to go through,

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:43.200
and that's okay. Those responses, I think, are all to be expected, and I appreciate, actually,

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:48.320
all of those. And, you know, if I could just take a moment here, I apologize because this is kind

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.580
of out of the ordinary, but I do just want to share to our church community who is here first,

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.400
and I actually have some words for those who are maybe past members of our church I want to share

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.800
after that. But I just want to share for those of you in our church community here, I know some of

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:07.780
you have been really confused or even hurt by things that you've seen or heard people say about

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.900
our church, maybe online or maybe just in other conversations. Some of you have heard people say

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:19.120
things about our church or about me or about our elders, and that's been confusing because to you

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:24.380
it just doesn't sound like our church community today. And you're wondering, where is all of this

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:28.900
coming from? And I just want to acknowledge to you that it's not coming out of nowhere.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.900
You know, some of you have felt angry on our behalf. Some of you have felt a desire to kind

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:40.520
of defend and stand up for our church. And I appreciate that. But also, I want all of us to

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:46.620
be aware that, and it's important to know, that there were some really unhealthy, hurtful, even

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:52.400
sinful aspects of our church culture in our history. Now, it's not that that's all gone today.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:59.480
It's not that there's no sin or no hurt in our church today. That would be unreasonable to think

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:05.460
so. As the famous quote, I forgot who said it, goes that the church is a hospital for sinners,

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:10.560
not a museum for saints. There's always going to be sin. But I do want to acknowledge that I think

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:15.900
there were some things in our history as a church where those sinful patterns and behaviors

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:22.640
became normalized, or justified, or even spiritualized. That this is actually the right

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:30.580
thing to do. And many of us were affected by that in a lot of ways. I can't go into every aspect of

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.680
that right now. It isn't the time or place. We're still going through that. But I want to just

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:39.360
acknowledge things like that in our history, there are people who felt just a lot of pressure

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:45.560
to conform to expectations. The weight of that was really heavy on some people, especially this

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:51.840
idea, well, you just don't question the leader. You don't question the pastor, especially. That

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:57.500
to question a pastor is almost to doubt God or something like that. That's what people experience.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:04.720
That's not true. I think out of some of that, there were people in our church who ended up

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:09.260
doing the things we did, the things that are valuable, even biblical things, but ended up doing

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:15.120
it out of fear of what people would think of them, fear of criticism, fear of maybe being thought of

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:20.640
in a certain way, rather than love for God and love for people, which is what God wants to motivate

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:26.780
us with. People experience that, and some people, I think, really felt used, even discarded, if they

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:33.020
didn't meet those expectations. I want to be clear that that's not everyone's experience. So many

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:38.440
people, again, messaged me sharing just positive experiences, stories like, man, God worked in my

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:44.300
life in this church. We can praise God for that still, and at the same time say that a lot of

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:51.340
people were affected by those things back then. Those who are angry and sharing that and expressing

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:57.880
that, whether publicly or privately, they're responding to what they experienced. And perhaps

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:02.840
they're even still assuming this is true of our church today. I just want to be clear with all of

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:06.360
us here in our church community, those who are sharing these things are not our enemies.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:13.700
They're our beloved brothers and sisters. And for many of them, they're hurt. And so I don't want

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:18.660
us to think of them as this is someone attacking our church. I want us to be able to just care for

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:24.100
and pray for them. We're not going to go out and fight with anybody. You know, the best way I think

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:28.420
for us right now to support and defend and build up our church is actually to pray for our church,

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:33.180
but also pray for those who are hurt. Pray for their healing and their restoration and for God

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:38.020
to be at work in their lives. So that's for our church community here, but also, you know,

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:42.440
if I could just speak for a moment to our former members. I know some of you might be checking in

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:49.600
on us today. If you're online, hi. I don't really have another easy way to contact you right now,

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:55.100
just briefly to share some things, but I do want to just start by saying if you were hurt by our

00:08:55.100 --> 00:09:00.200
church in the past, I apologize to you for everything that you went through. I just want

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:05.020
you to hear that. And by the way, if I could go back and preach last Sunday's message again,

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:09.240
I would acknowledge those things. I could have done that. I should have done that. I wish I did.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:12.980
I just want you to know we're listening to you

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.800
and we take your feedback seriously

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.380
there are some things I actually learned

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:19.440
from you this week that I never knew before

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.440
just through messages people shared with us

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:22.920
and I'm grateful to hear that

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:24.880
some of you have written some really helpful

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.060
thoughtful messages to us

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:28.340
that I deeply appreciate

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:31.140
and you know with hindsight of course at this point

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:33.120
if I could have gone back and just

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.820
done more of course I would

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.700
and I know many people would as well

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.540
but I just

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:41.100
want to acknowledge that and say

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.120
today I can't follow up on everything that

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.220
you've shared, but I know

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:47.220
some of you may hear

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:49.040
anything that I say or anything

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.820
someone in our church says with just

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.960
in the most cynical way

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.080
possible. And I just want to say I don't

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.080
blame you. I'm

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.500
again, not angry at you.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:00.960
I think that you're sharing

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.420
what you're sharing because you care.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:05.200
We want

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.100
to learn everything we can from this situation, not

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:12.680
just move on as if nothing happened, but we also can't make things happen instantly. A lot of the

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:17.180
changes we've already made in our church community have taken a long time and been really hard fought,

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.760
and processing all of this is going to take time as well. I just want to acknowledge that to you

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:25.460
today if you are listening, and say that we appreciate you, and we're praying for you.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:30.240
And that's something through all of this, if I can kind of transition us into today's message,

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:35.820
which feels really awkward now. But as we continue here, we're moving forward with the

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:40.300
life of our church. We have to continue wrestling with some of those things in the past. There are

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:44.320
people who were affected by our church in past years. I feel some responsibility to care for

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:49.680
them, and in whatever way, to try to respond to that. But also, I want to continue moving forward

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:54.100
with what God is doing here in our church today, and that's, you know, we've been going through

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:58.580
the book of Ephesians, and I think today's passage is actually really appropriate for where we are

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:02.460
today and what I think God's heart for us is today. We're specifically going to be focusing

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:07.120
on prayer, and I think we need a lot of prayer in our church community today. So if you've already

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:11.220
gotten to Ephesians chapter 1, what we're going to be focusing on today is that part of the higher

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:16.640
calling we've been talking about this year is for God, that God has for us, is to really be rooted

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:21.500
in prayer and depending upon God in prayer. So let me go ahead and read our passage today,

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:26.640
Ephesians 1 verses 15 to 23. Let me read this for us, and then we'll dig into the Word of God.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:32.220
For this reason, because I have heard of your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:37.320
toward all the saints, I do not cease to give thanks for you, remembering you in my prayers,

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:43.000
that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give you the spirit of wisdom and

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:48.240
of revelation in the knowledge of him, having the eyes of your hearts enlightened, that you may know

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:53.040
what is the hope to which he has called you, what are the riches of his glorious inheritance in the

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:58.060
saints, and what is the immeasurable greatness of his power toward us who believe, according to the

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:02.760
working of his great might that he worked in Christ when he raised him from the dead and seated

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:09.100
him at his right hand in the heavenly places, far above all rule and authority and power and dominion

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:14.980
and above every name that is named, not only in this age but also in the one to come. And he put

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:20.400
all things under his feet and gave him as head over all things to the church, which is his body,

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:25.600
the fullness of him who fills all in all. Let me pray for us one more time as we've read God's word.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.860
God, we invite you into this time that we spend together

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.280
as the family of the church today.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.620
And we thank you, Lord,

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.860
that we can be a spiritual family to one another

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:36.120
and that, Lord, that we can look into your word

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:37.740
and say, God, that we want to be formed

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:39.140
and shaped by your word.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.780
We want to be led by your word.

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.620
We want to be ministered to by your word.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:44.340
We want to be encouraged by your word.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.580
And Lord, today, we pray that you, through your word,

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.480
that you would guide us in our prayers

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:51.400
and that you would teach us how to pray

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.540
and teach us how to trust you to do the work in our lives

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.660
that only you can do.

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:58.440
And so please be with us here as a church family this morning.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:01.240
Be with our brothers and sisters at the undergrad retreat, God,

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:03.040
as they close out that time.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:05.860
And Father, help us to move forward as a church family together.

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:06.660
Thank you, God.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:08.080
It's in Jesus' name that we pray.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:08.640
Amen.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:09.780
Amen.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.540
Okay, so as we look into this passage here today,

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.700
I think it's a beautiful passage leading us into the kind of prayer

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:19.780
that God wants to see us live in in our church family.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:21.900
And today, just to give you a little bit of structure,

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:25.160
We're going to be talking this morning about prayer in a few different ways.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.980
We're going to start with talking about the motivation for prayer.

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:30.420
Then we'll talk about this as a model for prayer.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:35.340
And then we'll talk about having a ministry of prayer that the Lord wants us to live out

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:37.360
as part of the higher calling he has for us.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.620
So first, let's start with this idea of the motivation for prayer.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.520
I think for many of us, this is something that we struggle with.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:47.780
We struggle with the question, why should I pray or what should motivate me to pray?

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:51.860
We have that question in our minds as followers of Jesus in a lot of different ways.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:56.740
That's where I think it's helpful in starting this passage that Paul says, for this reason.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.000
And just so you know, Paul uses that phrase pretty regularly.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:04.760
When he uses that phrase, he's usually kind of bridging the thoughts before and after.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:08.860
It's kind of a transition from one thing to the other that pulls both together.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:10.540
And so what is he talking about here?

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.000
What is the for this reason?

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:19.480
Well, if you just look back at the couple verses before this, you'll see that part of this reason is because of their guaranteed inheritance.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.340
He says, this is part of why I'm praying for them.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.100
This is part of the motivation to pray.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.640
Just to read those verses for you again, it says,

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:32.720
In him you also, when you heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation, and believed in him,

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:41.420
were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit, who is the guarantee of our inheritance until we acquire possession of it, to the praise of his glory.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:46.340
And so, so far, we've already been going through Ephesians chapter 1 over the last few weeks.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:51.880
And many of you know that we're seeing already that our inheritance in Christ is sealed and

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:58.580
guaranteed by the Holy Spirit until we acquire possession of it. That means that this inheritance

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:04.560
is actually there waiting for us. And remember within that, when we talked about these verses,

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:10.840
we pointed out that that word guarantee actually is more properly translated as down payment,

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:15.560
and that the Holy Spirit is actually the down payment of our inheritance.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:19.100
It won't be fully received until God's heavenly kingdom comes.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:24.160
We can actually start living in that spiritual reality right now.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.860
Those things we've been talking about so far in Ephesians 1,

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:31.160
like how we can have a relationship with God as his adopted sons and daughters,

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:35.660
how we can live in forgiveness and freedom in Christ and unity and redemption,

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:37.220
all of those things.

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:41.800
And these resources are available to us in prayer.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:44.700
Now, I've just got to share a little side story about this

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:48.920
because we're going to talk about how do we access those resources in prayer.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:54.820
One resource within my household and my family that's really important to us is Diet Coke.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:58.120
It's a very important resource in our household, okay?

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:00.620
It's something we just need to know that it's there.

