00:32:38.610 --> 00:32:42.310
So Jesus came and died on the cross to pay the penalty of my sins,

00:32:42.350 --> 00:32:44.290
and now I have faith in him and trust him.

00:32:44.290 --> 00:32:46.970
I'm restored to relationship with God and eternal life.

00:32:47.290 --> 00:32:49.770
And yes, those are beautiful truths of the gospel,

00:32:50.150 --> 00:32:52.550
but at the end of the day, the story of the gospel,

00:32:52.670 --> 00:32:55.890
the message of the gospel is not just about you and I

00:32:55.890 --> 00:32:57.990
being restored to relationship with God.

00:32:57.990 --> 00:33:04.130
It is that Jesus Christ won victory over sin and death, was raised from the dead,

00:33:04.190 --> 00:33:08.830
and is now seated in glory in God's heavenly kingdom above all those authorities,

00:33:09.170 --> 00:33:13.190
above the whole universe, that he is the victorious one and is the head of the church.

00:33:13.370 --> 00:33:20.950
That is the power that Paul is now saying, I'm praying for this to be revealed to their hearts.

00:33:22.530 --> 00:33:24.090
Again, not just knowledge.

00:33:25.090 --> 00:33:28.270
I'm praying for this to be revealed to their hearts.

00:33:29.370 --> 00:33:31.690
You can't see this with your eyes.

00:33:32.710 --> 00:33:35.950
But can I ask you to think about how would it change your life

00:33:35.950 --> 00:33:38.870
if you could see that power with your heart?

00:33:39.790 --> 00:33:40.770
How would it change you?

00:33:41.790 --> 00:33:43.650
I was reflecting on this a little bit personally.

00:33:43.650 --> 00:33:47.930
I think if I could see this hope and power fully with my heart,

00:33:49.250 --> 00:33:52.810
well, I think I wouldn't be so easily discouraged or defeated by circumstances.

00:33:55.610 --> 00:33:58.250
I don't think things would bring me down so easily.

00:33:59.450 --> 00:34:01.790
If I could see this hope and power with my heart,

00:34:01.850 --> 00:34:03.950
I think I would have more courage and boldness

00:34:03.950 --> 00:34:05.570
to take steps of faith for the Lord.

00:34:06.310 --> 00:34:07.350
I wouldn't be so fearful.

00:34:08.570 --> 00:34:11.150
If I could see that hope and power with my heart,

00:34:11.230 --> 00:34:13.870
I think I would be more confident and secure

00:34:13.870 --> 00:34:16.690
in my identity in Christ, in my calling.

00:34:18.090 --> 00:34:20.190
And I think I'd pray with greater faith

00:34:20.190 --> 00:34:26.890
if I could really see that hope and that power of God with my heart.

00:34:28.760 --> 00:34:31.780
As we think about this, do you want this for yourself?

00:34:33.300 --> 00:34:37.180
Do you want this for others in your life who you love and care for?

00:34:38.240 --> 00:34:39.800
Does it make you want to pray?

00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:43.340
At least for me as I've walked through this, I want to pray.

00:34:43.460 --> 00:34:44.520
I want to pray for that.

00:34:45.340 --> 00:34:47.640
And so lastly, as we've already talked about this,

00:34:47.700 --> 00:34:50.540
as motivation for prayer and a model of prayer,

00:34:50.540 --> 00:34:54.620
can I then just talk to us about what a ministry of prayer could look like?

00:34:55.180 --> 00:34:57.720
What could a ministry of prayer look like for us?

00:34:57.980 --> 00:35:01.900
One thing I love about this passage is that Paul isn't teaching us about prayer,

00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:03.080
he's just showing us.

00:35:03.580 --> 00:35:06.400
And I think sometimes an example is a better teacher

00:35:06.400 --> 00:35:08.320
than just trying to explain something.

00:35:08.800 --> 00:35:13.220
Paul gives us an example here of what his ministry of prayer looked like.

00:35:13.260 --> 00:35:16.680
And I love it that in Paul's life we don't just see a ministry of teaching,

00:35:16.780 --> 00:35:18.780
that he went around just teaching everything and nothing else.

00:35:18.780 --> 00:35:24.340
We see him consistently through the book of Acts, through his letters, lifting up prayers for people

00:35:24.340 --> 00:35:31.640
because he knew his teaching, his leadership, his abilities were not going to bring people fully to maturity in Christ.

00:35:31.760 --> 00:35:37.160
It was only through all that with his prayers that God was going to do that spiritual work.

00:35:37.680 --> 00:35:42.960
And so what could this ministry of prayer look like for us, for those who we love?

00:35:43.120 --> 00:35:47.440
I'll just lay out a few things here as we reflect and as we close out our time together here.

00:35:47.440 --> 00:35:52.980
first thing. I think this ministry of prayer would look like praying biblically. Praying biblically.

00:35:53.360 --> 00:35:57.900
Again, today's message is one that you could actually pray every day for those you love.

00:35:58.300 --> 00:36:02.940
In fact, if you knew nothing else, but you just know, okay, I have some people in my life,

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:07.900
they already know Jesus. They already believe in the gospel. They already want to follow Christ,

00:36:08.300 --> 00:36:13.520
but maybe they're not fully mature yet, which are any of us fully mature yet? No. So I know some

00:36:13.520 --> 00:36:19.820
people. What could I pray for for them? If the only thing you did was just turn to this passage

00:36:19.820 --> 00:36:26.480
in Ephesians 1 and just pray this every day for those people that you know, that would be so

00:36:26.480 --> 00:36:31.920
powerful. And you know, maybe in that journey you find other passages of Scripture that are great

00:36:31.920 --> 00:36:37.300
models of prayer and you start praying those things out as well. That's huge. And what I think

00:36:37.300 --> 00:36:41.100
is so important about this is that I don't know what you shared earlier when you shared about

00:36:41.100 --> 00:36:45.120
like what do you tend to pray for, for people in your life who you love and care for. I think for

00:36:45.120 --> 00:36:50.500
me, honestly, there are a lot of times where my prayers are like, it's not bad, but I'll just pray

00:36:50.500 --> 00:36:57.140
for things like, you know, God, just help us have a good day today. You know, God, help my son do

00:36:57.140 --> 00:37:02.480
well in school, help Gina do well at work, help me, God, to be faithful with my responsibilities,

00:37:02.820 --> 00:37:07.300
you know, just prayers like that. And those are not bad prayers. But when we start to take the

00:37:07.300 --> 00:37:13.740
scriptures and say, God, I want to pray those things out, man, that is powerful. And I would

00:37:13.740 --> 00:37:18.680
encourage us, can we like say, God, I want to pray biblically and take these things in your word

00:37:18.680 --> 00:37:23.460
and start praying them for the people who I love. On top of that, I think it's really great to try

00:37:23.460 --> 00:37:29.240
to pray consistently. Notice in verse 16, it said, I do not cease to give thanks for you, remembering

00:37:29.240 --> 00:37:34.680
you in my prayers. That means that Paul was praying consistently for those he loved and cared

00:37:34.680 --> 00:37:39.680
for and praying regularly that God would work in their lives. I think it's really valuable for some

00:37:39.680 --> 00:37:44.760
of us here. Again, I don't know how we think about ourselves. Do you think about yourself as somebody

00:37:44.760 --> 00:37:50.500
like, I am a minister of the gospel of Jesus Christ. I am somebody who can have a ministry

00:37:50.500 --> 00:37:55.740
of prayer for those in my life. I think if we start to see ourselves that way, well then we

00:37:55.740 --> 00:38:00.640
might start to do things like block out time in our calendars and say, I'm going to set aside

00:38:00.640 --> 00:38:07.600
this time each day to pray for people, to pray for those who I want to see grow and live in the

00:38:07.600 --> 00:38:11.440
fullness of their inheritance in Christ. So I would encourage you with that. Maybe you want to

00:38:11.440 --> 00:38:15.800
put something in your calendar. Maybe it's even 10 minutes a day or 15 minutes a day to start

00:38:15.800 --> 00:38:20.980
and say, God, I'm going to use this time to pray and intercede for those who I love. I would also

00:38:20.980 --> 00:38:26.800
encourage you to pray confidently. Again, as we have talked about, this inheritance is sealed and

00:38:26.800 --> 00:38:32.120
guaranteed by the Holy Spirit. So we don't need to pray timidly saying, God, I'm not sure if you

00:38:32.120 --> 00:38:36.760
want to bless this person, but please do it anyway. God, I'm not sure if you want this person to grow

00:38:36.760 --> 00:38:42.760
to maturity, but maybe I could convince you. No, we know this inheritance is already given,

00:38:42.960 --> 00:38:48.380
already sealed, already guaranteed. The down payment has already been given. If we know that,

00:38:48.680 --> 00:38:53.660
that then that can cause us to pray confidently. And that's something that's so important because

00:38:53.660 --> 00:38:57.140
I think a lot of us here, maybe like myself, tend towards self-sufficiency.

00:38:57.720 --> 00:39:01.520
But I don't know about you, I don't want to see what I can do and what you can do.

00:39:01.600 --> 00:39:02.760
I want to see what God can do.

00:39:03.420 --> 00:39:05.800
And like M.Z. Dixon writes this, she says,

00:39:06.060 --> 00:39:09.440
when we depend upon organizations, we get what organizations can do.

00:39:09.700 --> 00:39:12.720
When we depend upon education, we get what education can do.

00:39:12.940 --> 00:39:15.340
When we depend upon man, we get what man can do.

00:39:15.500 --> 00:39:17.800
But when we depend upon prayer, we get what God can do.

00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:21.260
That's what I want to see.

00:39:22.220 --> 00:39:24.620
I don't just want to say, like, what I can do is not that great.

00:39:25.280 --> 00:39:27.120
What I can do is not powerful.

00:39:27.660 --> 00:39:30.920
But what God can do, and that's what I want to see.

00:39:31.300 --> 00:39:33.380
So can we pray with confidence that way?

00:39:33.700 --> 00:39:35.460
And also as we do that, pray desperately.

00:39:36.380 --> 00:39:37.100
Pray desperately.

00:39:37.420 --> 00:39:42.400
You know, I appreciate in this passage that Paul's tone in today's passage is very hopeful

